// Chapter 16, section 16.3 — the date table. Modeling > New table, then Table tools > Mark as date table (on 'Date'[Date]).
// Built in five steps in the chapter; this is the finished formula. Write the table as 'Date' in other formulas.
Date =
ADDCOLUMNS (
    CALENDAR ( DATE ( 2023, 1, 1 ), DATE ( 2025, 12, 31 ) ),
    "Year", YEAR ( [Date] ),
    "Month No", MONTH ( [Date] ),
    "Month", FORMAT ( [Date], "MMM" ),
    "Year Month", FORMAT ( [Date], "yyyy-MM" ),
    "Quarter", "Q" & QUARTER ( [Date] ),
    "Financial Year", "FY" & IF ( MONTH ( [Date] ) >= 4, YEAR ( [Date] ) + 1, YEAR ( [Date] ) )
)
// 1,096 rows. Sort the Month column by Month No (Column tools > Sort by column).
